Measured (oplog 09:16:50-09:17:23 and again 09:20:00): HOME fails -> WAR240007 jam NOTICE (kcode 0), then the blocking
ShowMyMessage "Motor not home yet!" (csystem.cpp DoHomeProcess). The HMI (dialog-bridge.js) shows one stop box at a time,
so the message box sat QUEUED behind the note, while MbWait held the note's dialog.notifyAck until that box closed
(NOTICE-DEFER-2): a deadlock, broken only by the page's 15 s ack timeout. Panel keys (RESET) wait in the same box.
Golden is strictly sequential (note ShowModal -> PAUSE closes it -> MyMessageBox).

Fix (tools/wb_serve.cpp, same lines): MbWait answers the notifyAck ok at once ({"notice":"held",...}) so the page
closes the note and draws the message box; the close work still runs after the box exactly as before (held, later
CompleteCommand on that id is a no-op -- WebBridgeServer::CompleteCommand returns when the ticket is gone). Not when
golden BtnPauseClick would refuse (W906_NoteNoticeAckRefusal != 0): then the note stays, as before. The global-scope
declaration goes on the existing :6554 declaration line (MbWait is in the unnamed namespace).

Debug compiled (wb_serve.exe link waits for EastSun's running program). ctest NoticeAck: passed. Code-after-comment scan: 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/wb_serve.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/wb_serve.cpp b/tools/wb_serve.cpp
index 86e437c..ce06f84 100644
--- a/tools/wb_serve.cpp
+++ b/tools/wb_serve.cpp
@@ -6551,7 +6551,7 @@ void ShowUnloaderTrayMessage(AnsiString S1, AnsiString S2);
 std::string W906MbIoDismiss();
 void W906_DialogCloseRequest(const char* channel, const std::string& requestId, unsigned long long requestSeq,
                              const std::string& actionName, int actionCode, const char* inputName);
-bool W906_SimDiCommand(const webbridge::WebCommand& wc);  bool W906_FastClockModalWait(webbridge::CommandQueue& q, unsigned long capMs);   // AI(W906-FASTCLK-MODAL) 20261003: FastClockWbServe.cpp -- declared at global scope HERE for MbWait's wait (:6760, inside the unnamed namespace: a block-scope extern there would bind to it, see :6518); same line
+bool W906_SimDiCommand(const webbridge::WebCommand& wc);  bool W906_FastClockModalWait(webbridge::CommandQueue& q, unsigned long capMs);  const char* W906_NoteNoticeAckRefusal(const char* requestId);   // AI(W906-NOTICE-DEFER-3) 20261007: + W906_NoteNoticeAckRefusal (forms/fNote_ShowError.cpp EOF) for MbWait's early notice answer, same reason.  AI(W906-FASTCLK-MODAL) 20261003: FastClockWbServe.cpp -- declared at global scope HERE for MbWait's wait (:6760, inside the unnamed namespace: a block-scope extern there would bind to it, see :6518); same line
 unsigned long long g_mbBlockingSeq = 0;   // MbPost 記下的「目前阻塞框」信箱 seq（Dialog-close-request 的 target.requestSeq）
 bool W906_IoPageNoGuards();   //AI(W906-IO-NOGUARD) 20260929: JsonBridge/IoBtnPanelClick.cpp; declared at global scope HERE (the MyMessageBox wait below is inside the unnamed namespace). Occupies a blank line
 namespace {
@@ -6822,7 +6822,7 @@ std::string MbWait(const std::string& qid, const char* const* opts, int nOpts)
                                                        (long long)wc.id, msAck, true);
                 g_modalServer->CompleteCommand((unsigned long long)wc.id, msOk, msAck);
             } else if (wc.cmd == "dialog.notifyAck") {   //AI(W906-NOTICE-DEFER) 20261003: EastSun「我歸原點後 有異常 排除後再按歸原點 就沒用了」-- 21:56:31 the PAUSE on the motor jam NOTICE came while the "Motor not home yet" box waited and was refused modal-pending: the notice stayed open (the page had closed it) and every later HOME key read "擋關：通知框開著" (golden ScanKey ignores keys while the note is up). Not refused any more: carried to the main loop, which runs it (and answers it) as soon as this box closes
-                w906NoticeHeld.push_back(wc);   //AI(W906-NOTICE-DEFER-2) 20261004: held, handed to g_carry when this wait returns (the w906NoticeHeld line at the top of MbWait); was g_carry.push_back + g_carryRunnable
+                w906NoticeHeld.push_back(wc);  if (wc.hasTag && ::W906_NoteNoticeAckRefusal(wc.tag.c_str()) == 0) g_modalServer->CompleteCommand((unsigned long long)wc.id, true, "{\"notice\":\"held\",\"requestId\":\"" + wc.tag + "\",\"runsWhen\":\"" + qid + " closes\"}");   //AI(W906-NOTICE-DEFER-3) 20261007: EastSun「這畫面我按pause 10秒後才有反應」/「我按reset 畫面很久alarm才會被清除」-- the page shows one stop box at a time and kept "Motor not home yet" queued behind the jam note until this ack was answered, while this wait held the ack until that box closed: a deadlock broken only by the page's 15 s timeout. Now the page gets ok at once (note closes, the box shows, as golden: note PAUSE -> MyMessageBox); the close work itself still runs after the box (held below; its later CompleteCommand on this id is a no-op). Not when golden BtnPauseClick would refuse (the note must stay).   //AI(W906-NOTICE-DEFER-2) 20261004: held, handed to g_carry when this wait returns (the w906NoticeHeld line at the top of MbWait); was g_carry.push_back + g_carryRunnable
                 std::printf("  [MyMessageBox] %s 等待中收到通知框的 PAUSE（dialog.notifyAck）-> 框關掉後由主迴圈處理\n", qid.c_str());
             } else if (wc.cmd == "act.home.abort") { ::W906_HomeAbortCommand(*g_modalServer, wc);   /*AI(W906-HOMEMON) 20261001: Abort Home answered during the MyMessageBox wait too, like motor.stop above (JsonBridge/ChanHome.cpp; :: = the file-scope declaration at :439, this wait is in an anonymous namespace)*/ } else if (wc.cmd == "io.btnPanelClick" && ::W906_IoPageNoGuards()) { ::W906_DispatchIoClick(*g_modalServer, wc); } else if (::W906_StateRecordDuringDialog(*g_modalServer, wc)) { } else {   //AI(W906-IO-NOGUARD) 20260929: IO click served during the MyMessageBox wait too.  AI(W906-S24-Q93) 20261004 (St02-E; Steven Q93 = A): State Record during this box
                 if (wc.cmd == "modal.answer" || wc.cmd == "dialog.response")   // 答錯對象（例如舊的一則）—— 印出來，現場查「按了沒反應」用
